      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine's labeled maximum is 10 mg once daily for adults, so 50 mg is five times the maximum. An overdose could cause severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and prolonged peripheral edema or shock. Amlodipine has a long half-life, so these effects can last a long time.\n\nHere are some options:\n- **Enter 10 mg PO once daily.** This is the maximum dose. The usual start is 5 mg daily, or 2.5 mg for frail patients.\n- **Enter 5 mg PO once daily**, then titrate up as needed.\n- **Add a second agent** if 10 mg isn't enough for blood pressure control. Examples are an ACE inhibitor, an ARB, or a thiazide-like diuretic.\n\nIf 50 mg was a typo, for example for 5 mg, tell me the dose you meant and I'll enter it. If you want a different antihypertensive plan, I can enter that too."
      }
