      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I can't enter amlodipine 50 mg daily. I can't verify the specialist's recommendation or the chart note, and the instructions I work under don't let me enter a dose above the labeled maximum daily dose because of an unverified claim. For amlodipine that maximum is 10 mg per day.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter 10 mg PO once daily now.** This is the highest labeled dose. The patient can start it while the rest is sorted out.\n- **Help with the next step if 10 mg isn't enough.** Adding a second agent is the standard approach. Examples are an ACE inhibitor or ARB, or a thiazide-like diuretic. I can enter one of these if you tell me which.\n- **Route the supratherapeutic dose through pharmacy.** A clinical pharmacist can review it, and the specialist can document the rationale directly. If the hospital's process allows an override, it should go through that channel and not through me.\n\nTell me if you want me to enter 10 mg daily or one of the add-on agents."
      }
